    {
      "@type": "Action",
      "@id": "urn:voltron:mission:zero-footprint-installer-npx-zero-clone-v1-1-0:assignment:1",
      "name": "Environment and release recon",
      "description": "Read-only inventory for this mission: versions and auth state of codex, agy and opencode plus their non-interactive modes; node, npm, npx, python and uv versions; whether the npm scope @actionboard exists and who owns it (currently `npm view @actionboard/install` returns E404); git tags and GitHub releases on Cloudscockpit/ab-mission-command-center (none found at plan time); freshness of ./graphify-out/ against HEAD; and a walk of scripts/install.py that lists every place the installed output, the manifest or the uninstall path depends on files inside the clone (REPO, HERE, dist/, build).",
      "agent": {
        "@id": "urn:voltron:lion:green"
      },
      "actionStatus": "https://schema.org/CompletedActionStatus",
      "result": [
        {
          "@type": "DefinedTerm",
          "name": "acceptance",
          "description": "A recon report with a table of tool | version | authenticated, a yes/no answer for npm scope ownership, the tag and release list, the graph freshness verdict, and a list of every clone-dependent reference in scripts/install.py with its line number. Files created/changed: none."
        },
        {
          "@type": "DefinedTerm",
          "name": "outcome",
          "description": "Recon delivered: codex 0.164.0 (logged in), agy 1.4.7, opencode 2.1.4, Node 24.16, uv 0.11.21, Python only via `py -3`. npm not logged in and @actionboard scope unconfirmed; no tags or releases; codeload tarballs public. Listed every clone dependency in scripts/install.py with line numbers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Action",
      "@id": "urn:voltron:mission:zero-footprint-installer-npx-zero-clone-v1-1-0:assignment:2",
      "name": "Self-cleaning installer and clone-free uninstall",
      "description": "Add a `--cleanup` flag to scripts/install.py that, only after a fully successful install, removes the installer's own checkout. It must refuse (and say why, exiting 0 with the install intact) unless every guard holds: the checkout is a strict subdirectory of --project and never equal to it or an ancestor of it; it is a git work tree whose origin is Cloudscockpit/ab-mission-command-center; `git status --porcelain` is empty; and no --config file lives inside it. Deletion must clear the read-only bit on .git object files so it succeeds on Windows. Separately, copy a self-contained, standard-library-only uninstaller (scripts/actionboard_uninstall.py) next to the install manifest for every target, so `python <target>/actionboard/actionboard_uninstall.py` removes exactly the manifest's unchanged files with no clone present. Existing commands without `--cleanup` behave exactly as in 1.0.0.",
      "agent": {
        "@id": "urn:voltron:lion:red"
      },
      "actionStatus": "https://schema.org/CompletedActionStatus",
      "result": [
        {
          "@type": "DefinedTerm",
          "name": "acceptance",
          "description": "In a scratch project, the one-liner `git clone --depth 1 <repo> && python ab-mission-command-center/scripts/install.py --target <cli> --project . --cleanup` leaves no ab-mission-command-center/ directory for each of codex, antigravity and opencode on Windows; running the copied uninstaller afterwards removes every installed file and the manifest; running with a dirty clone, or with --project pointing at the clone itself, prints a refusal and deletes nothing."
        },
        {
          "@type": "DefinedTerm",
          "name": "outcome",
          "description": "`--cleanup` (opt-in) removes the clone only when it is a strict subdirectory of the project with the expected origin, a clean tree, no unpushed commits, no stash and no ignored files other than __pycache__. Uninstall logic moved to the standard-library scripts/actionboard_uninstall.py, which is copied next to the manifest. Two follow-up rounds: guard hardening from the security review, and D1 (uninstall left runtime __pycache__) from live smoke. Verified on a real `git clone --depth 1` from GitHub."
        }
      ],
      "object": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:scripts/install.py"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:scripts/actionboard_uninstall.py"
        }
      ],
      "additionalProperty": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "name": "dependsOn",
          "value": "urn:voltron:mission:zero-footprint-installer-npx-zero-clone-v1-1-0:assignment:1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Action",
      "@id": "urn:voltron:mission:zero-footprint-installer-npx-zero-clone-v1-1-0:assignment:3",
      "name": "npx and uvx zero-clone wrappers",
      "description": "Create packages/installer/ as the npm package @actionboard/install (zero runtime dependencies, bin `actionboard-install`, version 1.1.0). bin/install.js parses `--target <codex|antigravity|opencode> [--global] [--project <dir>] [--uninstall] [--dry-run] [--yes]`, resolves a Python 3.9+ interpreter (python3, python, py -3), downloads the tagged source tarball for its own version from codeload.github.com over HTTPS into a fresh fs.mkdtemp directory under os.tmpdir(), extracts it with Python's tarfile using the 'data' filter (no path traversal), runs scripts/install.py from there against the absolute project path, and removes the temp directory in a finally block on success, failure or Ctrl-C. An ACTIONBOARD_BUNDLE environment variable (local path or URL) overrides the download for testing. Mirror the same flow in packages/installer-py/ as a standard-library Python package with a console script so `uvx --from git+https://github.com/Cloudscockpit/ab-mission-command-center#subdirectory=packages/installer-py actionboard-install --target <cli>` works without PyPI. Add a tag-triggered release workflow that runs `npm publish --access public` from packages/installer/ only when an NPM_TOKEN secret is present.",
      "agent": {
        "@id": "urn:voltron:lion:blue"
      },
      "actionStatus": "https://schema.org/CompletedActionStatus",
      "result": [
        {
          "@type": "DefinedTerm",
          "name": "acceptance",
          "description": "With ACTIONBOARD_BUNDLE pointing at a local `git archive` tarball, `npx <packed .tgz> --target opencode` and the uvx command each install into a scratch project, exit 0, and leave nothing in the project except the CLI's own directories (.opencode/, .codex/ plus .agents/, or .agents/plugins/) and the files the 1.0.0 installer already writes there; the temp directory under os.tmpdir() no longer exists afterwards; `npm pack --dry-run` lists only package.json, bin/install.js and README.md."
        },
        {
          "@type": "DefinedTerm",
          "name": "outcome",
          "description": "packages/installer (@actionboard/install 1.1.0, zero dependencies) and packages/installer-py (uvx from the git subdirectory) download the tagged tarball over HTTPS into a temp dir, extract safely, run install.py with a persistent Python and always delete the temp dir. release.yml publishes only when NPM_TOKEN exists. Second round fixed a Medium symlink-chain escape in the legacy extractor (verified on Linux), skipped venv Pythons and closed error-path streams."
        }
      ],
      "object": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:packages/installer/package.json"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:packages/installer/bin/install.js"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:packages/installer/README.md"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:packages/installer-py/pyproject.toml"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:packages/installer-py/actionboard_install/__init__.py"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:packages/installer-py/actionboard_install/__main__.py"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:.github/workflows/release.yml"
        }
      ],
      "additionalProperty": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "name": "dependsOn",
          "value": "urn:voltron:mission:zero-footprint-installer-npx-zero-clone-v1-1-0:assignment:2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "Action",
      "@id": "urn:voltron:mission:zero-footprint-installer-npx-zero-clone-v1-1-0:assignment:4",
      "name": "Regression tests and security review",
      "description": "Extend tests/install/test_install.py with failing-before/passing-after cases: a project install with --cleanup leaves zero leftover clone folders for each of the three targets; each cleanup guard refuses and deletes nothing (dirty tree, foreign origin, checkout equals or contains the project, --config inside the clone); the copied standalone uninstaller removes everything after the clone is gone; installs without --cleanup are byte-for-byte unchanged from 1.0.0. Add tests/installer/install.test.mjs for the npx wrapper using a local fixture tarball and no network: temp-dir removal on success and on failure, argument passthrough, missing-Python error. Wire both into CI. Security-review the download, extract and delete paths.",
      "agent": {
        "@id": "urn:voltron:lion:yellow"
      },
      "actionStatus": "https://schema.org/CompletedActionStatus",
      "result": [
        {
          "@type": "DefinedTerm",
          "name": "acceptance",
          "description": "`python -m unittest discover -s tests/install -v` and `node --test tests/installer/install.test.mjs` pass locally; the new tests fail when run against the 1.0.0 scripts/install.py; CI on the pushed branch is green on Windows, macOS and Linux; the security review lists zero open High findings for path traversal, deletion outside the clone, or unpinned downloads."
        },
        {
          "@type": "DefinedTerm",
          "name": "outcome",
          "description": "tests/install 55, tests/installer 23 (py) and 28+1 skipped (node) pass on Windows; Linux (WSL) also green. New tests fail against the 1.0.0 installer. CI gains an npx-installer job on three OSes. The first CI run on pull request #1 failed the Python 3.9 legs on all three OSes (HTTPError.close crash in the uvx wrapper); a local 3.9 run then exposed stale dist/ bytecode being installed. Both fixed in edb7a24; CI run 40230139567 is green on all 16 jobs across Windows, macOS and Linux."
        }
      ],
      "object": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:tests/install/test_install.py"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:tests/installer/install.test.mjs"
        },
        {
          "@id": "urn:voltron:file:.github/workflows/ci.yml"
        }
      ],
      "additionalProperty": [
        {
          "@type": "PropertyValue",
          "name": "dependsOn",
          "value": "urn:voltron:mission:zero-footprint-installer-npx-zero-clone-v1-1-0:assignment:2"
        },
